{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00055",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 2.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Right, come in and get settled."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.37,
      "end_seconds": 4.07,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hello."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.53,
      "end_seconds": 6.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "What seems to be the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.26,
      "end_seconds": 17.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.29,
      "text": "Mainly acne. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.96,
      "end_seconds": 21.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.6,
      "end_seconds": 28.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "About... well, nearly five years. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.4,
      "end_seconds": 31.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "What makes it worse, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.27,
      "end_seconds": 40.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Well, uh, oily food definitely sets it off. Oh, and oily skin. That's been about the same, about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.66,
      "end_seconds": 44.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.34,
      "end_seconds": 46.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.96,
      "end_seconds": 50.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "What about dark marks after they heal, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.41,
      "end_seconds": 55.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Yeah, yeah. Three weeks, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.17,
      "end_seconds": 70.63,
      "duration_seconds": 14.46,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.15,
      "end_seconds": 73.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.53,
      "end_seconds": 77.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Any pregnancy, new face cream or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.41,
      "end_seconds": 80.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.03,
      "end_seconds": 85.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.74,
      "end_seconds": 94.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 96.29,
      "end_seconds": 107.35,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature is 37.0 degrees, pulse is 66 beats a minute, BP is 121 over 69, SpO2 99 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.01,
      "end_seconds": 108.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.52,
      "end_seconds": 112.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.85,
      "end_seconds": 113.59,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.82,
      "end_seconds": 126.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Alright, do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.49,
      "end_seconds": 131.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.43,
      "end_seconds": 135.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.95,
      "end_seconds": 138.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.94,
      "end_seconds": 141.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.51,
      "end_seconds": 146.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.54,
      "end_seconds": 148.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.13,
      "end_seconds": 155.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "I used to smoke but I quit five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.56,
      "end_seconds": 160.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.55,
      "end_seconds": 161.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.24,
      "end_seconds": 182.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Let's go through your medication. What are you taking? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.33,
      "end_seconds": 186.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Metformin, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.5,
      "end_seconds": 188.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.67,
      "end_seconds": 190.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "500 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.55,
      "end_seconds": 195.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.46,
      "end_seconds": 208.84,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.86,
      "end_seconds": 215.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.04,
      "end_seconds": 225.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "I mean, I've had diabetes, yes. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.53,
      "end_seconds": 230.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known diabetes. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.99,
      "end_seconds": 234.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.08,
      "end_seconds": 235.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.52,
      "end_seconds": 247.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.02,
      "end_seconds": 251.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "My sister has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.43,
      "end_seconds": 265.0,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.62,
      "end_seconds": 268.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.3,
      "end_seconds": 274.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.31,
      "end_seconds": 276.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.82,
      "end_seconds": 278.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.11,
      "end_seconds": 301.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "There are red papules and a few pustules over the cheeks and chin, with some blackheads."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.5,
      "end_seconds": 303.2,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.3,
      "end_seconds": 314.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.1,
      "end_seconds": 317.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Hold on, the screen's frozen for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.77,
      "end_seconds": 353.1,
      "duration_seconds": 21.33,
      "text": "Good, where were we. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is moderate acne. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had acne for nearly five years, and no pregnancy or new face cream."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.67,
      "end_seconds": 356.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Hmm, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.0,
      "end_seconds": 359.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.71,
      "end_seconds": 364.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Hmm, yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.39,
      "end_seconds": 375.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "I'd like you to take adapalene gel, at night, for eight weeks. That's for acne. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.66,
      "end_seconds": 378.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Okay, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.03,
      "end_seconds": 399.96,
      "duration_seconds": 20.93,
      "text": "It takes six to eight weeks to see the difference, so please don't give up in the first fortnight. Don't squeeze them, that's how the marks stay. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.5,
      "end_seconds": 412.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. I'd like to see you again in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.5,
      "end_seconds": 417.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.05,
      "end_seconds": 423.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.16,
      "end_seconds": 431.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "So, I take the adapalene gel, at night and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 432.39,
      "end_seconds": 436.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 437.97,
      "end_seconds": 442.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    }
  ]
}